        "id": 1000294
      },
      "writtenOn": "2012-07-11T11:42:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will happen most of the time. Will it send a second stop bit? The datasheet says that this might happen.\n\nSee https://gerrit.chromium.org/gerrit/#patch,sidebyside,26832,1,chip/stm32/i2c.c\n\nI think we need a way of knowing that we have already sent a stop bit, and so don\u0027t send another one until a timeout has expired, or perhaps until the second time around the loop.",
      "revId": "070cc1738b9dffd44153b83710a3065e66a88476",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
